    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40799" root="هأ" body-key="h">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِىْءٌ</span></b> , subst. from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَأْهَأَ</span>, [<i>A call to camels to food,</i>
or <i>provender</i>]. (S, K.) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِىْءٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِىْءٌ</span> are said
to be thus written by Az's own hand, with kesr:
and are thus written in the Jáme' [of Kz]. (L.)
[See arts. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جأ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جيأ</span>.]

